{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.PawlowskiLeitnerInnerProduct","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.PawlowskiLeitnerInnerProduct","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.pawLei_pos_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.pawLei_pos_def","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L55-L60","doc":"Positive-definiteness: the PL inner product `⟨φ, φ⟩ > 0`\nfor any nonzero intertwiner `φ` (follows from `normSq_pos`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.normSq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.normSq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L53-L53","doc":"All basis norm-squares are positive — the orthogonal PawLei basis has\nstrictly positive norms, computed from hook lengths. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.normSq","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The norm-squared of each basis vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.num_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.num_basis","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Number of basis vectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PawLeiInnerProduct","kind":"structure","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L37-L53","doc":"The Pawlowski–Leitner inner product on intertwiner spaces.\n\nEach basis vector has a positive norm-squared.  The norms live in `ℝ`\n(the archimedean side of the substrate→archimedean wall, §7c): the\nnorm-squared `‖T_λ‖²` is the positive rational number computed from the\nhook lengths of the indexing Young tableau `λ`, so positivity is an\narchimedean order statement (`> 0`) and cannot be phrased over the\nordering-free ground ring `R_q`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:pawlowski-leitner-inner-product","label":"prop:pawlowski-leitner-inner-product","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/pawlowski-leitner-inner-product.lean#L29-L31","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}